**How to implement.** The source is real: a light source with a Stokes state and an intensity scale (001 §N 'The source is real: a source item with a Stokes state and an intensity scale'; 001 §I 'Light source | λ or tunable limits (exists) + output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) + an intensity scale'; the S8.1 brief: 'The source emits its own Stokes state x intensity scale'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, which opens `ItemModels`, gains before `RunStep`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `SourceEmission = { azimuth : Angle; ellipticity : Angle; degreeOfPolarization : ParameterValue; intensityScale : ParameterValue }`, the light a source emits. `member this.stokes : StokesVector` is I · [1, p·cos 2χ·cos 2ψ, p·cos 2χ·sin 2ψ, p·sin 2χ] with ψ the azimuth, χ the ellipticity angle, p the degree of polarization and I the intensity scale, written through `StokesVector.create` as `Propagation.inputStokes` writes its vectors (`Propagation.fs:inputStokes`); a positive χ is +S₃, the handedness `inputStokes` calls left, so a fully polarized source at azimuth θ and χ = 0 is `inputStokes IdealLinear θ` and one at χ = 45° is `inputStokes IdealCircularLeft`. The run law is unchanged in this step; step 252 makes it start from the emission. (2) `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `type ParameterValue with member this.angle : Angle`, the number read as radians (an `AngleParameter`'s unit, step 207). `type SourceEmission with static member ofValues (values : ParameterValues) : Result<SourceEmission, ItemEvaluationError>` checks the values against `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` (step 244, `checkedFor`, step 245) and reads the four through the `ParameterName` members, the two angles through `angle`. `ItemEvaluationError` gains `NotALightSourceErr of reason : string`, rendered `the model is not a light source: <reason>`. `type ItemModelChoice with member this.emissionWith (values : ParameterValues) : Result<SourceEmission, ItemEvaluationError>` is `SourceEmission.ofValues values` for a `SourcePresetChoice` (step 216) and `NotALightSourceErr` naming the model's kind for every other choice: the source arm of the one evaluator, which S8.2's source slot and S11.2's forward model call with the source item's values. The wavelength stays the preset's, as today. No other member is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`: `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale`: `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` answers azimuth and ellipticity 0, degree of polarization 0 and scale 1, whose `stokes` is exactly [1, 0, 0, 0] (`Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`). `a source emits its polarization state times its intensity scale`: a degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° with scale 2 emits 2 · `inputStokes IdealLinear (30°)`; ellipticity 45° emits `inputStokes IdealCircularLeft (0°)` and −45° `inputStokes IdealCircularRight (0°)`; a degree of polarization 0.5 at azimuth 0 emits [1, 0.5, 0, 0]; each component within 1e-15. `only a light-source model emits, and its values must be in range`: `(PolarizerPresetChoice (the PresetIds.polarizerLp polarizer)).emissionWith` of any values answers `NotALightSourceErr`; `(SourcePresetChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633)).emissionWith` answers the default emission over the defaults, `ParameterOutOfRangeErr` with a degree of polarization of 2, and `MissingParameterValueErr` without `ellipticity`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` (step 245) covers `NotALightSourceErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.

**Acceptance.** After the real source lands, `SourceEmission.stokes` MUST be the source's polarization state times its intensity scale, the default parameter set MUST emit unpolarized light of unit S₀, and only a light-source model MUST emit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale`, `a source emits its polarization state times its intensity scale`, `only a light-source model emits, and its values must be in range` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.
